    "id": "13b86f1b-537f-4158-88f5-9f6f66ec439e",
    "content": "On Windows 11, `npm link` creates symlinks/junctions that get blocked as \"untrusted mount points.\" Instead of fighting symlinks, write a direct `.cmd` shim (`node \"C:\\absolute\\path\\dist\\bin\\cmemory.js\" %*`) and a matching bash shim in the npm global bin directory.",
